    <div class="metalabel">The signature question</div>
    <h3>What does one human actually need?</h3>
    <p class="u-27">Instead of starting from ideology, Uncost starts from the physical and social basics of a dignified life — fifteen sectors, from Food and Shelter to Communication and Leisure. Every part of the essential basket maps to one of them.</p>
    <a href="/sectors/" class="u-28 u-btn u-btn--ink">All fifteen sectors</a>
    <p class="u-29">Regionality is built in: a single global cost number would damage credibility. Early versions cover only a few regions and label coverage plainly — for example, &ldquo;data available for three regions.&rdquo;</p>
